.TH SESSLINT-WATCH 1 "" "SessLint 0.5.0" "SessLint Manual"
.SH NAME
sesslint-watch \- [read\-only] Poll session directories and flag newly corrupted files.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sesslint watch [\-\-agent {claude,codex,all}] [\-\-interval SEC] [\-\-adapter {auto,canonical,claude\-code\-jsonl,codex\-rollout,openai\-agents}] [\-\-json] [\-q | \-\-quiet] [\-v | \-\-verbose] PATH...
.SH DESCRIPTION
[read\-only] Poll\-based observer: debounced mtime+size snapshots, emits one line per verdict transition. Pure observer — never writes, never installs hooks. Ctrl+C exits cleanly.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.B PATH
Path(s) to session file(s) or directories to watch
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-agent {claude,codex,all}
Watch a well\-known agent session root instead of paths Choices: claude, codex, all.
.TP
.B \-\-interval SEC
Poll interval in seconds (default: 2.0, min: 0.05) Default: 2.0.
.TP
.B \-\-adapter {auto,canonical,claude\-code\-jsonl,codex\-rollout,openai\-agents}
Session format adapter for all inputs (default: auto) Choices: auto, canonical, claude\-code\-jsonl, codex\-rollout, openai\-agents. Default: auto.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Emit sesslint.watch\-event/v1 NDJSON transition events
.TP
.B \-q, \-\-quiet
Suppress non\-error stderr output
.TP
.B \-v, \-\-verbose
Print debug diagnostics (settings provenance, elapsed) to stderr
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
a clean session exits 0
(also verification passed / dry-run plan generated)
.TP
.B 1
a session with findings exits 1
(also verification failed / repair refused)
.TP
.B 2
an internal tool error exits 2
(also usage error / invalid flags / I/O failure)
.TP
.B 130
Cancelled — interrupted via Ctrl+C or a cooperative cancellation request;
partial outputs are cleaned up.
.SH SEE ALSO
sesslint(1), sesslint\-bundle(1), sesslint\-check(1), sesslint\-completion(1).

.nf
Full documentation: the docs/ tree in the source repository
